[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 500,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 539,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71074,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 60,
        "headingId": 539,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Large cell neuroendocrine carcinoma (LCNEC) is a high-grade carcinoma consisting of large cells with prominent nucleoli, exhibiting neuroendocrine differentiation.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T16:04:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 501,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 540,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71075,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 60,
        "headingId": 540,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8013/3 Large cell neuroendocrine carcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T16:04:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 502,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 541,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71076,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 60,
        "headingId": 541,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C94.Y &amp; XH0NL5 Other specified malignant neoplasms of bladder &amp; Large cell neuroendocrine carcinoma</p>\r\n<p>2C90.Y &amp; XH0NL5 Other specified malignant neoplasms of kidney, except renal pelvis &amp; Large cell neuroendocrine carcinoma</p>\r\n<p>2C94.Y &amp; XH0NL5 Other specified malignant neoplasms of bladder &amp; Large cell neuroendocrine carcinoma</p>\r\n<p>2C9Y &amp; XH0NL5 Other specified malignant neoplasms of urinary tract &amp; Large cell neuroendocrine carcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T16:04:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 503,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 542,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71077,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 60,
        "headingId": 542,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T16:04:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 504,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 543,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71078,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 60,
        "headingId": 543,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T16:04:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71079,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 60,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LCNEC occurs in the kidney, bladder, prostate, and ureter; rarely, it can occur in the penis {22690881}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T16:04:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71080,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 60,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients with renal tumours most frequently present with flank or back pain and/or haematuria. Tumours from the ureter may occur with hydronephrosis, and bladder tumours usually have haematuria as a presenting symptom {32366387}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T16:04:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71081,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 60,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LCNECs are rare in all sites in the urinary tract, with &lt;&nbsp;10&nbsp;primary renal LCNECs and &lt;&nbsp;40&nbsp;primary bladder LCNECs having been reported.</p>\r\n<p>Prostate LCNEC has been seen almost exclusively in the context of prior androgen-deprivation therapy; its incidence is difficult to assess because of its rarity and confusion with other entities under the rubric of prostate adenocarcinomas with neuroendocrine differentiation {32366387; 31306859; 32850401; 24705311}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T16:04:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71082,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 60,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T16:04:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71083,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 60,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LCNEC in the prostate develops as a transdifferentiation of a castration-resistant prostate cancer upon androgen-deprivation therapy (especially with the newer AR signalling inhibitors) {31306859; 29297494}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T16:04:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71084,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 60,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Renal LCNECs are large (frequently &gt;&nbsp;100&nbsp;mm in diameter), in contrast to those in other locations that are between 10 and 90&nbsp;mm. In the bladder, tumours may be polypoid or nodular {31306859; 32850401; 23358695}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T16:04:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71085,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 60,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "<p>LCNECs of all locations in the urogenital tract have a similar microscopic appearance. Pure LCNECs are composed of cells with high-grade nuclei that show focal pleomorphism and frequent prominent nucleoli. These are arranged in a neuroendocrine architecture with nests, acini, and trabeculae. Many tumours may have an admixture with urothelial carcinoma or prostatic adenocarcinoma in their respective primary sites and should be labelled as mixed tumours.</p>\r\n<p>Immunohistochemically, tumour cells are reactive for chromogranin&nbsp;A, synaptophysin, and CD56 {30565306}. Mitoses are frequent, and the Ki-67 labelling index may be as high as 90%. AR is usually negative in prostatic LCNEC. PSA and PAP should be negative or weak in tumours originating from the prostate {31306859}. Thyroid transcription factor&nbsp;1 (TTF1)&nbsp;and cytokeratins may be expressed in LCNEC {28739749}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-05-04T17:35:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71086,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 60,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T16:04:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
